---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Standards & Archival Integrity | Arun Kumar Journalism"
  description="The editorial and archival standards governing the Arun Kumar living digital archive: faithful reproduction, multi-source verification, and permanent preservation."
>
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 860px; padding-top: 3.5rem; padding-bottom: 5rem;">
    <div style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border-color); padding-bottom: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
        <span style="display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #16a34a;"></span>
        <span style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: #16a34a; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">
          Living Integrity Standards
        </span>
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size: 2.75rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">
        Editorial Standards & Archival Integrity
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
        The principles and practices ensuring the continuous fidelity of Arun Kumar's active, ongoing journalistic body of work in this living digital archive.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
      <section class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color);">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">1. Word-for-Word Faithful Reproduction</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
          Every article published on this living digital archive preserves the original published journalistic text with 100% fidelity. No paragraph is summarized, paraphrased, or rewritten. All quotes, data points, bureau datelines, and investigative findings are maintained exactly as originally printed in <em>Hindustan Times</em>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid #0284c7;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">2. Multi-Source Verification</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          To safeguard against broken links and ensure long-term accessibility, each article is backed by multiple independent sources of verification:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <li><strong>Original Source:</strong> Direct link to the original article on <code>hindustantimes.com</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Permanent Archive:</strong> An independent, permanent snapshot preserved on the Internet Archive's Wayback Machine.</li>
          <li><strong>Print Record:</strong> High-resolution newspaper scans or official PDF clippings where available.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid #16a34a;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">3. Tamper-Proof Integrity</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
          At the time of archival, each article's content is digitally fingerprinted to create a unique record. This allows readers and researchers to independently verify that the text has not been altered since it was first archived — ensuring complete editorial integrity over time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid #9333ea;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">4. Author Verification</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
          To guarantee that only reporting by Arun Kumar (Associate Editor, Patna Bureau) is included, every article undergoes multiple layers of verification. Bylines are cross-checked, dateline locations are validated against Bihar and Patna, and article content is reviewed to ensure it falls within the correct reporting beats — preventing any mix-up with other journalists sharing the same name.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
